-kujo --version</code></pre><button class="sk-button" data-copy-code hidden>Copy code</button><span role="status" data-code-status></span></div><p>Save <code>print("Hello, Kujo!")</code> in <code>hello.kujo</code>:</p><div class="sample-code"><pre tabindex="0"><code>kujo check hello.kujo
-kujo run hello.kujo</code></pre><button class="sk-button" data-copy-code hidden>Copy code</button><span role="status" data-code-status></span></div><p>Expected output: <code>Hello, Kujo!</code>. <a href="/language/">Native installers, Windows guidance and troubleshooting</a>.</p></section>
-<section class="language-section"><p class="eyebrow">Ecosystem · installed separately</p><h2>Start with the job you need done.</h2><p>These are independent projects. Tools that inspect repositories or run configured commands can support existing languages; SDK code itself runs in Kujo.</p><div class="language-grid"><article><h3>Build an AI agent</h3><p>Use Agents SDK with AI SDK for Kujo agent programs.</p><a href="/ecosystem/agents-sdk/">Agents SDK</a></article><article><h3>Coordinate multi-step work</h3><p>Define repeatable work and inspect its state.</p><a href="/ecosystem/dispatch/">Dispatch</a></article><article><h3>Understand a repository</h3><p>Inspect existing code and assemble context for a change.</p><a href="/ecosystem/scout/">Scout</a> · <a href="/ecosystem/scent/">Scent</a></article><article><h3>Evaluate generated work</h3><p>Run configured checks and browser assertions for your project.</p><a href="/ecosystem/eval/">Eval</a> · <a href="/ecosystem/lens/">Lens</a></article><article><h3>Review a change</h3><p>Turn Git diffs and footprint into inspectable evidence.</p><a href="/ecosystem/patchbrief/">PatchBrief</a> · <a href="/ecosystem/changebucket/">ChangeBucket</a></article><article><h3>Prepare a release</h3><p>Evaluate repository readiness against explicit checks.</p><a href="/ecosystem/shipcheck/">ShipCheck</a></article></div><p><a href="/ecosystem/">Browse the full ecosystem</a></p><h3>From request to reviewable change</h3><ol class="workflow-stages"><li>Define scope</li><li>Retrieve context</li><li>Implement in a chosen environment</li><li>Run tests</li><li>Inspect change evidence</li><li>Assess readiness</li></ol><p>Composable stages, not an automatically integrated pipeline. <a href="/development-workflow/">Follow a reproducible repository workflow</a>.</p></section>
